  "execution": {
   "depth": "MoGe-2 through the product's MoGeDepthModel on this Mac's Metal (MPS) device, 228 photographs, through the machine-wide GPU slot; no remote or paid compute",
   "features": "pycolmap 4.2.0 SIFT on the CPU",
   "held_out_files": "every one of the split's 936 files checked against the digest taken when it was copied from the lane that rendered it, in the read-only copy and in the working copy the depth pass wrote into, before the run",
   "machine": "Apple M5 Max, macOS 26.7",
   "scripts": "the pre-registration's bound copies, run as they are bound: scripts/held3_run.sh.txt, in one run (held-out/run.log.txt), with one thread a process"
  },
  "findings": [
   "Carrying the lens did what it was for. Two joinable pairs were named changed in each arm, against version 1's six and five on the same photographs, and no pair was joined across a change or a move in either arm. The two are described next; neither was diagnosed as the lens.",
   "held3-courtyard-132-s3 (1, 2), joinable, named changed in both arms (2.36 and 2.38 percent): the camera moved 0.187 m, the estimate was 0.09 m with a sigma of 6 mm, inside the hand-held bound, and the depth-edge bands a movement of that size makes are narrower than what the true one uncovers. Version 1 refuses the pair too (4.17 and 3.42 percent).",
   "held3-landscape-332-c1 (1, 2), joinable, named changed in both arms (3.86 percent; version 1 3.66): the camera moved 2.6 cm and the added box's own surface is outside the pair's shared view, by both the surface measure and version 1's sphere. OBSERVED BY EYE after the run, not measured: the box's shadow reaches towards the view photographs 1 and 2 share. The truth this record defines counts a changed part's surfaces, not the light it blocks, and a person sees a shadow appear.",
   "held3-landscape-331-mv2 (0, 1), moved 1.24 m, named changed in both arms by every version: the translation was estimated at 0.20 m, inside the hand-held bound, from the depth model's scale in a landscape (not_covered in the pre-registration), so the camera was taken to have stood still and the view compared.",
   "held3-courtyard-131-c3 (0, 1), a box added over 34 percent of the shared view, named moved in both arms by every version: the translation was estimated at 1.2 m where the camera moved 6.5 mm.",
   "The naming rates fell under the thresholds version 2's development data set, for version 1 too: of the 28 moved pairs, 23 were refused for overlap, which the names allow and the rate does not count as named.",
   "The exif arm's misregistration failure comes from pairs version 3 joins and version 1 refused as changed: on the 106 pairs both versions arranged, the 95th percentile is 0.288 degrees for each. Its worst pair, held3-landscape-331-s3 (0, 1), a hand-held pair 0.14 m apart whose parallax is 2.99 degrees at the 95th percentile, was joined 1.66 degrees beyond it; version 1 named it changed (3.48 percent).",
   "Up is version 2's method, unchanged: 0.184 and 0.182 degrees at the median, 1.33 at worst, where version 1 leaned 1.47 at the median and 5.49 at worst.",
   "A set joined in 3.2 s at the median and 11.7 s at most in each arm, two arms at once on a machine other work was loading (version 1: 2.7 s and 4.5 s). An observation, not a budgeted timing."
  ],
